    <comment>shake-cursor is a lightweight X11 utility written in C that dynamically enlarges the mouse pointer when shaken rapidly (similar to the wayland and macOS &quot;shake to find&quot; feature).

Features: Automatically adapts to the active X11 cursor theme, provides smooth scaling, and includes a systemd user service for background execution.

This package improves desktop accessibility and cursor visibility on high-resolution displays (4K/Ultrawide) and multi-monitor setups for X11/XDG environments. It has no heavy dependencies, building only against standard X11/Xfixes/Xi and libinput libraries.</comment>
